https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z1-QLr6aBaw  (Capo 2)

Also available in (G) mainly for fingerpicking.

TIP:  There are many great covers of this old western tune.  This one is by Michael Martin Murphey from his album Cowboy Songs.  At the end there's an additional verse that is sometimes included in other versions but not in this version by Michael.   

TIP:  The opening is a harmonica playing the melody of the first three lines of the verse.  You can play the chords but it'll sound sweeter if you can pick out the notes on the high register (bottom 3 strings - largely from within the (D)) through "sunshine" and then finish with chord strums of the final sequence beginning with (G).   
   
    
